Spec: Repository Bootstrap

Platform: Bash/Spec Kit 1.0.10/Boundary

Purpose:
  Reproduce the tested development toolchain and install the Spec Kit change-system adapter through the same component installer used to prove local and immutable-archive packaging.

Owns:
  ./bootstrap.sh
  ./install.sh

References:
  ../integration/specdd/extension.sdd
  ../integration/specdd/workflow-overlay.sdd
  ../integration/specdd-preset/specdd-preset.sdd

Must:
  Bootstrap pins Spec Kit `1.0.10` and records upstream SpecDD CLI `1.1.1` as the migration compatibility baseline.
  Until SpecDD migration parity no longer requires typed intended-target resolution, bootstrap installs the temporary resolver provider from `https://github.com/dmos62/specdd-cli.git` branch `feature/resolve-intended-targets`.
  Temporary resolver-provider validation requires package version `1.2.0` and resolver support for `--file`, `--folder`, and `--sdd-file`.
  SpecDD compatibility dependencies belong to development migration checks rather than downstream Boundary adapter installation.
  Bootstrap does not run `specdd init` or require `.specdd/bootstrap.md`; legacy SpecDD state is not a source of normal Boundary agent instructions.
  The active Spec Kit integration is `codex` so adapter commands and task augmentation can be materialized under the tested Spec Kit `1.0.10`.
  Existing initialized repositories change active integration through supported Spec Kit integration commands.
  ./install.sh installs the Spec Kit adapter extension, small task preset, and project workflow overlay through supported Spec Kit lifecycle commands.
  ./install.sh materializes native Boundary runtime code as generated `.specify/boundary-runtime` state for the adapter wrappers.
  ./install.sh accepts the local checkout, a local archive, or an immutable GitHub tag, commit, or release archive as installation source.
  Remote installation rejects mutable GitHub branch archives.
  ./install.sh supports clean adapter removal, reinstall, and installation-health checks.
  The public Spec Kit adapter surface contains only `speckit.boundary.authorize` and `speckit.boundary.verify`.
  The workflow overlay owns implementation-entry authorization and implementation-exit verification without duplicated extension hooks.
  Planning and task work use on-demand Boundary inspection rather than persisted context or validation lifecycle states.
  Missing required host executables report dependency-specific remediation before bootstrap mutates repository state.

Must not:
  Initialize or require SpecDD framework bootstrap files merely to provide agent instructions.
  Require the SpecDD CLI for downstream Spec Kit adapter installation.
  Patch generated Spec Kit commands, installed extension state, installed preset state, or workflow-overlay state directly outside supported installation materialization.
  Use npm, PyPI, or a public Spec Kit catalog as the adapter distribution requirement.

Done when:
  Bootstrap apply followed by check succeeds with the tested development migration baseline while the installed Spec Kit adapter exposes only Boundary authorization and verification transitions plus exact task write metadata guidance.
  Local checkout installation and immutable GitHub archive installation use the same native Spec Kit component operations and generated Boundary runtime materialization.
